---
seoTitle: "About GameNews"
seoDescription: "Original upcoming-game features and official publisher news, with clear sources and dates."
---

GameNews follows upcoming games and official gaming announcements. Our editorial features help readers decide which games to keep on their radar and which questions to ask before launch.

## How our features are made

Our features are AI-assisted, source-based editorial articles. They link to official publisher material and state when information was checked. They are not hands-on reviews, benchmarks, or promises about final quality. We do not label a game as trending without dated evidence.

## How automatic news works

The Game Updates section checks the official Steam announcement feeds for our selected games. It creates clearly labeled automatic update briefs on GameNews from announcement metadata and a limited source preview. Each brief links to the publisher's complete post. We do not republish full articles or turn announcements into hands-on reviews.

The feed checks when you visit, every 15 minutes while the page is open, and when you return to the tab. Source publication dates remain visible. When a source is unavailable, a dated saved copy may be shown with a notice. A new announcement becomes a new brief; an older post keeps its original date. Our longer editorial features remain publication-dated snapshots and are updated separately.

## Images and links

Genuine publisher artwork is identified with credits and source links. Any illustrative generated artwork is labeled separately. Copyright remains with the respective rights holders; GameNews is not affiliated with the publishers it covers.

We do not host game files or app installers. Product links lead to official sources.
